# C++ and MFC code (Envy)

Global rules (style, read-only trees, banned constructs) are in `AGENTS.md`.

## Language level
- C++20 policy, but live Release|x64 Envy, HashLib, TorrentEnvy and Unpacker
  end their `ClCompile` block with `stdcpp17`: keep that code C++17-clean
  until a dedicated vcxproj change removes the override.
- Prefer small local modernization: `nullptr`, `override`, `constexpr`
  instead of `#define`, `noexcept` instead of `throw()`, range-for when it
  reads better, `std::optional` for missing values.

## Ownership and lifetime
- RAII for handles, sockets, locks and buffers; no new manual `new`/`delete`.
- Raw pointers are non-owning unless the owner is documented.
- `const&` inputs; move only when ownership transfers.

## MFC conventions
- `C` + PascalCase classes, PascalCase methods, `On...` handlers.
- Members: `m_s` strings (not `m_str`), `m_n` numbers, `m_b` flags (`BOOL`
  in MFC members), `m_p` pointers, `m_h` handles, `m_t` times, `m_o` objects.
- `CString` and `_T("...")` in UI/MFC code; Unicode (UTF-16) paths.
- Shared state: existing `CCriticalSection` / `CSingleLock` / `CQuickLock`
  patterns. Never block the UI thread; never touch UI controls from worker
  threads (use `PostMessage`).
- Includes: in `.cpp` files of projects that use the `StdAfx.h` precompiled
  header, include it first, then the file's own header; never add it where
  the project has none, and do not reorder legacy includes.

## Errors
- Check Win32/MFC/WSA results; keep the error code and the context (operation,
  file, peer).
- `ASSERT` for debug invariants, `VERIFY` when the call must run in release.
- User-visible errors via `theApp.Message(MSG_ERROR, ...)`. Never swallow
  errors silently; never throw from destructors.

## Performance
- Profile before optimizing. In hot paths avoid per-iteration allocation and
  logging, reuse buffers, pre-size containers, avoid repeated `CString`
  concatenation, batch UI updates.
